It would help if you'd read the post you were replying to,
rather than arguing against something that was never said.  I
said "it depends", arguing against the (common) advice to always
use daggers.  So you show a case where daggers are to be
preferred.  How does that contradict "it depends".

All other things being equal, arrows do more damage.  But being
nethack, all other things are almost never equal---I use bow and
arrow in some cases, and daggers in others.

> The *only* difference occurs when the bow does multiple shots
> per round - *if* they hit. Just to make it *absolutely* clear,
> the dagger ranges from 4 to 7 whereas the arrow 1-7.

> Now *how* do you figure arrows do more damage?

Because you don't always have the strength bonus, and any time
beyond the mid-game, you should be hitting 100% of the time,
regardless.  At equal skill level, without the strength bonus,
arrows do more damage.  Of course, by mid-game, you should also
have strength of at least 18, which makes them about even.

> You are welcome to use the charts/instructions at the bottom
> of weap343.txt to show your work.

Elven ranger does at least as well with arrows as with
daggers---his choice should really depend on what he finds the
most of.  And obviously, any class which can advance bow higher
than dagger does better with it.  As for barbs: they may not
have a reputation as a spell caster, but attack spells are still
what works best at range for them.  (At high experience levels,
magic missle can be extremely potent.)

